### WHEELS — everything about wheels lives here

#### Positions — get this wrong and you send a part that can't fix the problem

| Position | What's there | What swaps in |
|---|---|---|
| **Front** | Swivelling casters. What "catches," "sticks," or "stops on uneven ground." | V1 upgraded front wheels $32 (**V1 silver frame only**). On V2 the only front fix is the all-terrain 4-pack. |
| **Rear** | Fixed wheels. | **Stair climbing $42 (2x) · Beach $42 (2x)**. Both are REAR PAIRS. |
| **All four** | — | The **all-terrain 4-pack**, the only set that replaces the fronts on a V2. |

**A front-wheel complaint is never solved by stair or beach wheels.** They go on the back.

#### The catalog

| Wheels | Price | Fits | URL |
|---|---|---|---|
| V2 upgraded all-terrain 4-pack | — | V2 Shopper | **Not back. No date.** See below. |
| V1 upgraded front | $32 | V1 Shopper, front only | `stroleecarts.com/products/upgraded-stability-shopper-front-wheels` |
| V2 stair climbing | $42 | V2 Shopper only (black frame) | `stroleecarts.com/products/v2-stability-shopper-stair-climbing-wheels` |
| V2 beach | $42 | V2 Shopper only (black frame) | `stroleecarts.com/products/v2-stability-shopper-beach-wheels` |
| Double/Baby+ v2 upgraded | $59 | Double v2, Double Lite, Baby+ v2. **Baby site only.** | `stroleecarts.com/products/upgraded-wheels-for-strolee-double-baby-v2` |
| Destination upgraded set | $50 | Destination only (2 front + 2 rear) | `stroleebaby.com/products/destination-upgraded-wheel-set` |
| Clearance stair climbing | $22 | **Original Shopper & Beach Cart ONLY** | on `collections/accessories-all` |
| Clearance beach | $28 | **Original Shopper & Beach Cart ONLY** | on `collections/accessories-all` |
| Rear street wheels, v3 Beach Cart | $29 | Beach Cart | on `collections/accessories-all` |

*Availability checked 2026-08-22 on `stroleecarts.com/collections/accessories-all`: all of the above
in stock except the 4-pack. There is **no standard replacement wheel** sold separately for the V2.*

The **V1 upgraded front wheels ($32)** are ball bearing, about 20% larger in diameter than the
originals, tool-free install. The only upgrade wheel a silver-frame V1 owner can use.

#### Hard compatibility facts

- **Stair and beach wheels are V2 only** (black frame). They will not attach to a V1 silver frame.
- **A V1 owner cannot have stair wheels at all.** The clearance stair set is Original Shopper and
  Beach Cart only. There is no stair option for a V1, and the only route to one is a V2 cart. Say
  that plainly rather than implying a workaround exists.
- **Why, and it's a good answer:** we were working on making them fit the V1 frame and found it
  **would have compromised the frame's stability**, so we built them for the new frame instead
  rather than make that trade on a cart people lean on. Say "would have," not "did," so it stays
  about the design we didn't ship rather than the cart in their house. *(Atira, 2026-08-22.)*
- **Original Shopper owners: we DO still sell wheels for it.** The clearance listings, $22 and $28,
  in stock. They sit on `accessories-all` rather than the front of the site, which is why customers
  write in saying we only sell wheels for the beach and stability carts. Send the collection link.
- **The Personal Shopper has no upgraded or all-terrain set any more and there is no substitute.**
  Clearance is **leftover stock, not an upgrade**. Don't relabel it as "the sturdiest option that
  fits your cart." Say we don't make upgraded wheels for that cart any more, say sorry for the news,
  lay out what we have, let them choose. *(Atira, 2026-08-22: "be honest with franchesca about what
  were offering. we do not have the upgraded wheels.")* **This generalises: when we don't have the
  thing, we don't have it.** Offering the nearest remaining item is fine; dressing it up as the
  thing they asked for comes back as a second ticket.
- **V1 rear wheels need tools** and can't be swapped for any upgrade wheel. V2 rear wheels are
  tool-free.
- **Beach Cart wheels are Beach Cart only**, different mounts, not interchangeable with Shopper.

#### Handling

- **Wheels come off with a silver tab, not a button.** A small **silver tab** where each wheel meets
  the frame. **Press and hold it and the wheel slides straight out.** No tools. *(Atira, 2026-08-22:
  "it's not a button." The stair-wheel product page and some past replies say "push a button to
  release." That wording is wrong, don't copy it.)*
- **Rear axle swap:** push the small silver tabs both sides, slide the old out, slide the new in.
- **Front wheel "broken" or won't turn:** it's bound in the frame. Hold the silver tab and pull the
  wheel out to release it.
- **Front wheels lift or wobble when empty:** normal with no weight in the seat.
- **Brakes "don't work" with stair wheels on:** by design. Brakes work with standard, beach and
  upgraded wheels. A feature question, not a defect.
- **Stair wheels on steps and curbs: they pull the cart behind you**, gripping each step as it goes.
  They stay on for flat ground, no swapping back. V2 stair wheels work on all surfaces indoors and
  out.
- **The caster lock is a Personal Shopper feature.** Do **not** tell a Stability Shopper owner to
  check their swivel lock. Confirm with Shad before giving any front-wheel mechanism advice on a
  Stability Shopper.

#### Video and links — the two traps

- **A wheel swap is shown on the stair-wheel product listing, below the add to cart button.**
- **Send that link only to someone actually asking about the stair wheels.** It is a $42 product
  page. Dropping it on someone who asked how the wheels come off reads as a pitch and implies they
  need that product. For a plain "how do I remove the wheels," the answer is the silver tab and
  nothing else.
- **Don't attach a link because it's adjacent.** A product link inside an answer tells the customer
  they need that product. Link what they asked about, or nothing.
- **Never conclude a video doesn't exist from a page fetch.** Fetching returns text, not embedded
  video. Product listings carry videos below the add to cart button. If you can't confirm, ask
  rather than telling a customer we don't have something.

#### The all-terrain 4-pack — the cohort, and what they've been promised

The factory sent the wrong wheels. Pre-orders were **canceled and refunded** across a whole cohort,
several of whom bought the cart *because* of those wheels. Everyone affected has been promised a
**discount code plus free shipping** when the set returns, expected **around mid-September**.

Known affected: Michelle Beach, Sally Yantis, Theresa Barnett, Monica Bauman, Victoria Vega.

What they've already been told: Abbey promised **free shipping** (2026-08-08); Atira said **about a
month** with a **code sent by email** (2026-08-17). Don't now tell those customers there's no date,
and don't drop the free shipping or the code. Before answering any upgraded-wheel ticket, assume
they're in this cohort and check what they were already promised.

