### Replacement parts we do NOT sell

*Checked 2026-08-22 on stroleebaby.com.* There is **no replacement seat cover, seat fabric, seat
cushion, canopy, or seat liner** for the Double. The only Double accessories are the Parent Organizer
($55), Rain Cover ($49.90), Snack Tray ($19.90), Snack Cups, and Carrying Straps (from $9.90). If
fabric damage isn't covered under warranty there is nothing to link them to. Don't offer one.

### Shipping and carriers

**Where they're made:** *"These are manufactured in our partner facility in Asia & shipped from our
warehouse in Charlotte, NC."* That exact wording is the standing answer, used across at least seven
tickets. Say **manufacturer**, never supplier. *(Confirmed 2026-08-24.)*

Ships from the **Charlotte, North Carolina warehouse**. Warehouse only, no storefront pickup.
**US only, no Canada.** Carts ship to **residential addresses only**.
Overseas customers have two routes: the EU storefront `stroleecarts.eu`, or **shipping to a US
address themselves and forwarding it on**. Take the second if they suggest it, it's a normal US order.

| | |
|---|---|
| Carts and strollers | **FedEx** (default) |
| Some Strolee Baby orders | **UPS**, also often used for reshipments |
| Small accessories and parts | **USPS**, can be requested for a replacement part |
| Hawaii and Alaska | **FedEx SmartPost** (FedEx hands to USPS for the last mile). Biggest source of chronic delays. Large surcharge. |

**Always verify the actual carrier on the order before naming one.** The archive has a customer
told two different carriers on consecutive days, and a Hawaii order that went UPS rather than
SmartPost.

- **Ships 1-2 business days**, **3-5 business days** in transit. "Most orders arrive within about a
  week."
- **Shipping cost:** $8.95 on carts, **free over $300**. Strolee Baby standard ~$6.95.
- Boxes often arrive **opened and retaped**. That's us adding purchased accessories, not damage.
  Say so plainly.
- **Accessories ship inside the stroller or cart box** — adapters, wheels, seat liners, organizers.
  Check there before treating anything as missing.

### Discounts, promotions and payment

**When a customer is ready to buy, lead with yes.** Answer the compatibility question, name the
offer, offer to set the code up. Don't volunteer the shipping threshold, don't do the price
arithmetic for them, don't front-load a small no into a sale. Atira's version, 2026-08-22, in full:

> Yes, your shopping bags, cooler bags, rain cover and organizer all work on the stability cart! We
> do have upgrade offer is $40 off, and you keep the cart you have! And we have black in stock! If
> you'd like that I can set up a code for you!

**Codes never stack. One discount per order**, and checkout keeps the larger one. When a customer
expected two, the fix is to manually refund the dollar difference. Free shipping over $300 is a
separate threshold, not part of the stacking rule.

| Program | Terms |
|---|---|
| Military / first responder / teacher | **15% via GOV-X** ID verification, same rate for all three. Cannot combine with any sale or code. |
| Birthday | 15%, single use, auto-issued. **Not reissued once expired**, even for high spenders. |
| Welcome / email signup | $15-$20 off |
| Senior | **None exists.** |
| HSA/FSA | Through **Burst** only. See Part 3. |

**Standing amounts:** **$30 goodwill / retention / exception. $40 V1 upgrade.** Anything above is
Atira's call for that ticket only and never gets written in here as policy.

**Price adjustments: we do match.** Cheaper elsewhere or on sale right after they buy, refund the
difference to the original payment method. **30-day window**, refused past it. We don't match a
bundle broken into one component, don't match a discount a third-party channel funded itself, and
don't stack a price match with an additional percentage off. Amazon orders aren't visible to us, but
they can reorder on-site and get matched.

**When a code fails:** clear cookies and cache, close all browsers, try incognito. If it still
fails, have them place the order and send the code after for a manual refund of the discount.
Expired codes are reissued generously, including hand-made one-offs. A code failing on part of an
order is usually a minimum-spend gate or the stacking rule.

**Payment:** card, PayPal, Apple Pay, and **Shop Pay** including installments (2-12 months).
- **Affirm is discontinued.** Existing Affirm customers contact Affirm directly.
- No Klarna, no Afterpay, no phone, money order, or prepaid card.
- Installment providers are third-party. We can't see or edit payment details or resolve plan disputes.
- **An apparent double charge is usually one failed authorization plus one successful charge.**
  Verify before assuming. The system auto-merges identical duplicate orders.
- **PayPal auto-fills the shipping address from their PayPal default.** A recurring cause of
  wrong-address tickets, and not something we control.
- **A chargeback blocks everything** — no direct refund, it goes through PayPal's process and they
  usually have to cancel the chargeback first. An active dispute can block future orders.

### Restocks and launches — one answer, no dates

For anything not yet on the site, or out of stock with no date: **"we'll announce it by email."**
No date. No offer to personally email that one customer.

**The exception is someone already owed something specific** — a refunded pre-order, a photo we said
we'd send, a code we promised. Those keep their personal notification, and their tickets stay open
carrying it.

**Don't contradict a date already given to that person.** Check the thread first.
**Nothing to draft if the event hasn't happened and we've already told them.**

Current items: the **all-terrain 4-pack** (see WHEELS) · the **top tray** (see Accessories) · the
**seated cart, "about a year or two"** (Atira, 2026-08-18 — that's the answer on record, don't be
vaguer or more precise than it).

### Links that come up constantly

- Stability Shopper how-to: `stroleecarts.com/pages/stability-shopper-how-to` — holds **Assembly**,
  **Lower Pet Carrier Install**, **Car Seat Adapter Install**, plus the HSA/FSA section. **No video
  on the site for using stair-climbing wheels on steps or curbs.**
- Personal Shopper assembly / fold: `stroleecarts.com/pages/personal-shopper-assembly` — holds
  Caster Locking · Unfolding · Locking Brake · Shopping Basket · Lower Storage Basket.
  **Only ever for someone who actually owns a Personal Shopper.**
- Pet stroller assembly (bassinet fold at 1:30): `stroleecarts.com/pages/pet-stroller-assembly`
- Beach cart assembly: `stroleecarts.com/pages/beach-cart-assembly`
- Double V2 how-to (kickstand at 2:40): `stroleebaby.com/pages/strolee-double-v2-how-to`
- All accessories and wheels: `stroleecarts.com/collections/accessories-all`
- Warranty: `stroleecarts.com/pages/warranty` · `stroleebaby.com/pages/warranty`
- HSA/FSA: `stroleecarts.com/pages/fsa-hsa`
- Military/first responder/teacher: `stroleebaby.com/pages/govx-id-military-discount` ·
  `stroleecarts.com/pages/military-discount`
- 30-day home trial: `stroleebaby.com/pages/30-day-home-trial`
- EU storefront: `stroleecarts.eu`

### Contact

No phone line. Email `connect@stroleecarts.com`, web form `stroleecarts.com/pages/contact`,
address 480 Interchange Dr, Dallas, NC 28034.
When someone asks for a phone number: *"We don't have a phone line, but I'm right here and happy to
help you work through it!"*

---

## PART 3 — DECISION PATHS

### WHAT STROLEE CAN AND CANNOT DO — check before drafting, not after

| Situation | The limit |
|---|---|
| Delivered to the address they entered, not received | **Cannot reship.** Customer opens the case with the carrier. |
| Wrong address entered at checkout | **Almost never** reshipped or replaced, especially high-ticket. |
| Return | Original packaging with tags, tested indoors only. **Shipping both ways comes out of the refund.** Refund within 5 business days of arrival back. |
| Warranty | **Manufacturing defects only.** Photo **and** order number first, every time. |
| Store credit | Available, and preferred over a refund. |
| HSA/FSA | **Cannot** apply it or process reimbursement. Burst only. |
| Airline handling | **Cannot** promise gate check is free or cover transit damage. |
| Discount codes | Explain the offer and link the product, **don't create the code** until they confirm. |
| Cancel **before** it ships | **Yes, on request. No fee, no cutoff clock.** The cutoff is physical carrier pickup. Full refund, 1-5 business days. |
| Cancel **after** it ships | **No.** No recall, no paid intercept. **Never tell a customer to refuse delivery.** Wait for arrival, then a return label. |
| Cancel **after** delivery | Not a cancellation. Converts to a return. |
| Goodwill / retention / exception | **$30 standing.** Above that is Atira's, per ticket. Don't improvise a number. |
| Restocking fee | **No set fee**, but the refund can be reduced for condition. Wording rules under Returns. |
| What comes out of a refund | The **actual outbound shipping charge**, varies by carrier and distance. Archive runs $7 (accessory, USPS) to $39; carts generally $30-$45. Don't quote a fixed number. |
| Anything outside these | Atira's call. Draft the reply, flag the decision, don't commit us. |

### Order changes, cancellations and addresses

**Before it ships — say yes.** No fee, no questions, no time limit. An order can be pulled back even
after the shipment notification email goes out, so a notification is not a reason to refuse.

Routinely done pre-ship: color swap, model swap, adding or removing accessories, applying a missed
discount code, and **merging two orders so they pay one shipping charge**.

- **Price went up** on a swap: email a Shopify invoice for the difference, ships once paid. Shipping
  is not re-charged.
- **Price went down:** partial refund to the card.
- **Missed a discount at checkout:** apply the code and refund the difference. Don't cancel and reorder.
- **Shipping holds** are available, adjustable any time, released on confirmation.
- **PayPal chargeback blocks the refund.** We can cancel, but can't refund until they withdraw it.

**After it ships — no cancel, and don't invent options.** Say what we do instead: wait for it to
arrive, then we send a return label. Offering the label proactively is the norm. Additions become a
separate order.

**Address change before it ships:** routine, free, done at the warehouse.

**Address change after it ships: we cannot do it.** *(Settled by Atira 2026-08-21.)* Don't offer to
try, don't file a request with the carrier, don't promise an attempt. The 2026 archive has agents
attempting it with FedEx and UPS. That's retired.

What the customer can do themselves:
- **UPS:** change it through the UPS virtual chat. Send them the tracking link.
- **USPS:** only if they already have package forwarding enabled.
- **Tracking lags any accepted change.** The package can keep showing the old address, or even move
  toward it, before updating. Say so up front or it generates a second ticket.

**Wrong address the customer entered:** their cost, no free reship. Two options: return label plus a
new order, or return and reship at their expense (~$35-$55 plus reshipping). Tell them to price a
carrier-direct forward first and only use us if it's cheaper. Be warm but direct, clarify the facts,
and **don't leave the door open** for a resolution from our side. Closing: **Take care.**

### Delivery problems — three cases, three different answers

**Verify before you remedy.** A large share resolve as "found." First reply confirms the shipping
address on the order, sends the carrier's delivery photo, and asks whether there's a building office
or front desk and who signed.

| What tracking shows | What we do |
|---|---|
| **Delivered to the address they entered** | **No reship, no refund.** They open the case themselves with their tracking number (FedEx 1-800-463-3339 / fedex.com). Closing: **Take care.** |
| **Stalled, lost, or never scanned** | **We reship free**, or refund in full if they'd rather wait no longer. Say which it is and let them pick, in one message. |
| **Carrier never attempted, returning to sender** | **Ours to fix.** Reship free. Switching carrier on the reship is reasonable if they ask. Don't make them open a case for a package coming back to us anyway. |
| **Package came back to us** | **Returned / undeliverable / no reason given → reship it** (284138955, 258353800; verify the address first if anything looks off, 269468908). **Customer REFUSED delivery → refund it** (256766698), and they're welcome to reorder. |

**Stalled tracking is not "delivered but not received."** If the last scan is days or weeks old and
it was never marked delivered, that's a lost shipment and we reship free.

**Don't concede when they say the carrier blamed us.** Once it's in the carrier's hands, the carrier
investigates.

**Blocks on any reship:** an open chargeback, or an order already refunded.

**Confirm the shipping address before any reship.** Always, even when the order shows one and even
when the address was never the problem. Ask, get it back in their words, then send. *(Settled by
Atira 2026-08-22.)* **Name the carrier off the order, never off memory.**

**Porch theft: we do nothing.** Confirmed delivery to the address they entered, then taken, is not
ours. No reship, no refund, no discount. Warm, direct, no door left open.

*Policy note: through about March 2026 Strolee opened carrier cases itself and reshipped or refunded
at its own cost. That stopped. Use the current posture, not the old tickets you'll find in search.*

### Missing item from a shipment

**Our problem, not the carrier's — the opposite of a lost package.**

**We are usually not missing things.** *(Settled by Atira 2026-08-22.)* Treat it as "it hasn't been
found yet," not "we failed to pack it." Do not open by conceding, do not lead with a free
replacement.

**Check-first covers every item.** Wheels, adapters, bags, organizers, all of it. The cart ships
fully assembled with the wheels packed loose, so a wheel in the box padding is exactly what gets
missed. The parent cup holder settles into the lower basket and blends in, the number one
missing-item ticket, and most resolve as found.

**Use this wording.** From macro **262668**, 223 uses, picked by Atira over a draft of mine because
it *"sounded more pleasant."* Match this register for any item:

> Thanks so much for reaching out and I would be happy to assist! Can you please just confirm it is
> not in the lower basket for me? Many times in shipping the cup holder ends in the lower basket &
> blends right in so people don't notice it at first :)- I look forward to hearing back getting this
> resolved for you.

What makes it land: it **asks a favor** rather than issuing an instruction, and it **normalizes by
blaming shipping and the object**, not the person. It doesn't front-load the remedy.

If it's genuinely missing: **reship the piece free. No return, no photo, no waiting period.**
Common false positive: the item was never on the order. Quote the order lines and offer an invoice.

Closing: **Talk soon.**

### Wrong item shipped

**Ask for photos of what they received before offering any remedy.**
- **Our error, low-value:** ship the right one immediately, they keep or dispose of the wrong one.
- **Our error, high-value:** prepaid return label emailed and the replacement arranged. We pay return shipping.
- **They ordered the wrong thing:** normal return terms, refund reduced by actual shipping both ways.

### Damaged in transit

**Photos or a short video are mandatory before any remedy.** No exceptions, both shops, every agent.

Ladder, in the order actually used:
1. **Self-fix if it just came apart in shipping.** Small screwdriver down the tube to pop the silver
   snap piece out, then slide together until it clicks. Resolves a lot of them.
2. **Replacement part, free** — belly bar, snack tray, footrest, wheel, cup holder, bassinet, liner
3. **Full replacement unit.** Strollers require a photo of the **safety harness straps cut off**
   first. Hard safety gate, never waived. Carts generally need nothing back.
4. **Partial refund instead of a replacement** — archive shows $20, $25, $50, $75
5. **Full refund or return**

- **Damaged box, undamaged product = no remedy.** Ask them to open it and confirm first.
- **Past 30 days it's warranty only** (replacement part), not a return or refund.
- **Free and gift items aren't replaced** if the product still works safely.

### Delays

Actionable the moment tracking shows no movement or a stalled scan.
- **Expedited paid but not met:** refund the **difference** between what they paid and standard, not
  the whole amount.
- A delay that will miss their date is grounds for cancel and full refund pre-delivery, and a late
  arrival has been accepted as a return reason.

### Warranty

**2 years from purchase**, standard on every product. **$24.99 buys an extension to 5 years total**
(not 2+5), can be added after shipping by emailed invoice and removed with a refund on request.

- **No registration exists.** Tracked digitally against name, address or order number. Tell
  customers there's no paperwork to keep, they ask constantly.
- **It does not transfer.** Secondhand owners aren't covered. Say so, offer the paid path.
- **Amazon orders are honored** with an Amazon order ID.

**Covers manufacturing defects only, and that applies to every part equally** — belly bars, wheels,
buckles, frames, all of it. There is no list of covered and uncovered parts. The archive looks
contradictory (a belly bar sent free one week, sold for $17.90 the next) only because the real
question was never the part.

**The real question is always: does the evidence show a manufacturer defect?** A judgment call on
the photo or video. The test used in past replies is **arrival condition**: "if it had come like
that we would have replaced it." Something that broke in normal use after months is not the same as
something wrong out of the box.

**Not covered:** customer-caused damage, pet damage, mold from storage, normal wear, secondhand and
resold units. Decline with a paid path forward, never a bare no.

**Required before processing — all four:**
1. **A photo or short video of the problem.** Carts: video *from the side* so the locking mechanism
   is visible. Folding complaints: video of the fold attempt.
2. **Order number. Hard requirement.** *"We need her order number."* — Atira, 2026-08-22. A name, an
   old email, or "I bought it last July" is **not** the order number. Those are leads for a lookup,
   and the lookup has to actually happen and come back with a real order before anything ships.
   Until then the claim is incomplete, and a draft saying "that's everything I needed" is false.
3. **Confirmed current shipping address** — these often changed since purchase.
4. **Whole-unit stroller replacements only: a photo of the seat belt straps cut off. Mandatory, no
   exceptions, ever.** An insurance requirement, not waivable, however sympathetic the ticket.
   Nothing ships until the photo is in hand. The old unit is not returned, they dispose of it.

**When the order genuinely can't be found and the part is small: offer the $3 shipping invoice.**
Atira's wording: *"Or since it's such a small piece we can send you an invoice for $3 just to cover
shipping and since we can't tie it to an order in our system."*

**What ships free:** any defective part, or the whole unit. **No dollar threshold** — full strollers
and carts at $195-$369+ ship free under warranty. Next business day, 2-4 days transit.

**If the model is discontinued and no parts remain:** no free replacement. Offer a discount on the
current model, they keep the old unit. Archive range: **$40 off carts, $50-$60 off Baby+/Linq/beach,
$100 off Double Lite, $150 off Double V2.** Where the warranty is live but the exact model is gone,
send the current-generation equivalent free instead.

**Customer buys:** belly bars ($17.90), upgraded wheels, accessory bags and organizers, add-ons.

### Most common failures — what actually breaks

Ranked by replacement parts arranged, Jun 2025 to Aug 2026:

| Rank | Part | Tickets |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Harness buckle / clasp** | ~100 |
| 2 | Rear axle | ~45 |
| 3 | Wheels (front most often) | ~40 |
| 4 | Whole stroller or cart | ~35 shipped free |
| 5 | Snap buttons | ~20 (plus many resolved by the pen fix) |
| 6 | Belly bar | ~18 (mostly sold, not replaced) |
| 7 | Frame | ~10 |

The harness buckle is number one by a wide margin, and the most common trigger for a whole-unit swap
because the buckle housing isn't separately replaceable on older models.

### Known fixes — try these before authorizing anything

Every one of these closes a ticket with nothing shipped. **Never open with "nothing's wrong with
it."** Give the instruction, then leave the door open for it genuinely being faulty.

**Snap buttons / "I'm missing screws."** There are **no screws anywhere**. Small spring-loaded metal
buttons on the **UNDERSIDE** lock frame parts together. Always tell them to look underneath.
- Sequence: press the button all the way in with your thumb, **hold it**, slide the piece on, keep
  sliding until the button reaches the hole and **pops out on its own**. That pop is the click.
  Never tell them to line the button up with the hole themselves.
- Say the button pops **OUT**, never "up."
- **Stability Shopper cross bar (manual step 3):** the buttons are on the underside of the bars **on
  the cart**, not on the cross bar. The two halves of the cross bar slide together and don't click
  into each other; the click comes from the cart's buttons.
- **Common cause:** the button slipped down inside the tube during shipping, so there's nothing to
  press. Drop a pen or screwdriver into the open end and push gently, it pops back out.
- Approved comparison: "the same kind of spring button that holds a collapsable tent pole together."

**Stroller won't stand up** (one of the highest-volume tickets). The kickstands ship stowed so they
don't get damaged and need releasing. Push the small bar in, rotate 180°, it drops into place. The
Double has one per side, singles have one. Re-stow before gate checking.
**Always include the link and the timestamp:** `https://stroleebaby.com/pages/strolee-double-v2-how-to`,
**shown at the 2:40 mark**. Kickstands genuinely do arrive bent or missing (284843999, 284844789, 269453583,
286717635), so don't open by saying nothing is wrong. Give the instruction, then offer: if it still won't come out, send a video.

**Cart won't stand:** the two small bars below the handle slid in during shipping. Pull them out further.

**Cart won't open:** lift the handle **all the way**. Not lifting fully is the common failure.

**Cart won't fold:** lift the handle slightly *and* squeeze the handle button at once, then push
**forward and slightly down**, not backward. On carts with a green arrow button: green arrow unlocks
it to roll, the handle button folds it.
Folding on the Stability Shopper and Pet Stroller (same frame): lift the handle slightly, squeeze
the handle button at the same time, the whole cart folds forward and clips in place when flat.
**Send `stroleecarts.com/pages/stability-shopper-how-to`.** Never send `personal-shopper-assembly`
to a Stability Shopper owner, that's a discontinued product and it tells someone with a current cart
to follow instructions for a cart that isn't theirs.

**Won't clip open — cart (Stability Shopper):**
1. Fully release the button on the handle
2. Push the handle down and back slightly, a quick swift "snap" motion helps
3. Try it with the shopping bag removed so the latching mechanism is visible
4. The small piece needs to go inside the larger piece to clip open
*(Reference photo in Gorgias macro 220545.)*

**Won't clip open — single / Baby+:**
1. Fully release the button on the handle
2. Push the handle down and back, quick swift "snap"
3. While it extends, don't just let the front wheels smack the ground
4. If it's open but not clipped: thumb on top of the handle, pointer finger behind it where it goes
   down toward the seat, clip it open that way

**Won't clip open — Double:** Gorgias macro 285887 has a troubleshooting video.

**Stroller won't open:** quick upward snap, thumbs in front of the handle, index fingers behind. The
latch is the small circle directly under the handle.

**"It collapses / it won't lock":** **if red is showing at the side locking mechanism it is not
locked. No red = locked.** Test by flicking the handle or pushing the basket down while holding the
handle. Strollers show a red bar on the side when open and locked.

**Wheels, axles, brakes, front wheels:** see the WHEELS section in Part 2.

**Nuna car seat won't seat:** set it onto the adapters from behind, lined up, then squeeze the foot
area slightly and it slides in.

**All latch tickets:** troubleshoot before offering a return. If troubleshooting doesn't resolve it,
ask for a photo of the latching mechanism. Never affirm the product is unsafe or defective.

### Wheel complaints (bumps, rough surfaces, tipping)

Do **not** affirm the complaint, agree there's a flaw, validate tipping claims, or offer upgraded
wheels free. Don't breeze past what they said either, that reads as dismissive. Approved phrasing:

> The standard wheels that come with the stroller are designed for smooth, everyday surfaces. For
> parents who are more active and out on all kinds of terrain, we created the upgraded wheel set as
> an add-on. They were designed specifically for surfaces like sidewalks, parks, and rougher outdoor
> areas so you get a smoother, more comfortable ride.

Never compare the current part unfavorably to the upgrade ("handles curbs much better" is out).
Frame it as a lifestyle choice, not a fix. Which wheels actually fit: see WHEELS in Part 2.

### Air travel

Carts do **not** fit in an overhead bin (V2 Shopper folds to 25.5" tall, that's what rules it out).
They can take it through the airport and gate check it. Strollers, Destination and Linq, **do** fit
overhead bins.
- **Never promise gate check is free.** Fees and policies vary by airline. Tell them to check with
  their airline.
- **Never imply airline damage is covered.** Once it's in the airline's hands Strolee doesn't cover
  transit damage. Say so plainly and kindly.

### Returns and refunds

**Read the delivered date off the fulfillment record, not the ship date.** On a Shopify fulfillment
`created_at` is when it shipped; the delivered date is the later timestamp once `shipment_status`
reads `delivered`. Using the ship date makes an order look older than it is. Check it every time
before telling anyone they've missed the window.

**The window is 30 days from DELIVERY.** Enforced hard, denials cite tracking and order timestamps.
A customer who asked a question inside the window but didn't act does **not** keep it open.
Pre-orders start the clock when the item arrives. **This holds even when we were the ones waiting on
them.** *(Confirmed by Atira 2026-08-22.)*

**Past-window recovery offer: $40 off a Beach Cart, and we do not exchange.** Say the window has
closed, say it kindly, then put the offer in front of them. Exceptions past the window are **very
rare** — judgment, kept tight. Store credit or the **$40-off V2 upgrade** (they keep the old cart)
are the other recovery routes.

**Eligibility — pass/fail, not negotiable:**
- **No original box = automatic no.** Not one exception in the archive. The box is a custom size and
  the cart can't be resold shipped in anything else. Say the reason, it lands better than the rule.
- Tags and safety information intact, item new and resalable
- **Tested indoors only.** Used outdoors = no. Used at all = no.
- **Open Box carts are final sale**, returnable only if genuinely defective
- **Amazon orders return through Amazon**, never through us
- **Promo and bundle orders come back whole**, free items included
- Standard wheels included in a stroller's price can't be returned separately

Failing a condition can mean a **reduced refund** rather than a flat refusal. That's a real option.

**Shipping comes out both directions, at our actual carrier cost, not the $8.95 they paid.** The
$8.95 is a partial subsidy, and free-shipping orders are still charged the real cost. Typical
deduction **$32-$45 on a cart or stroller**; accessories as low as $7. Don't publish a fixed number.
*Reference point: a $519 two-stroller order (SB13574) refunded $443.74, so $75.26 came out.*

**We eat the shipping when** the returned item inspects as defective (full refund including
shipping), or on compassionate grounds like a death in the family.

**Restocking and condition — the wording matters.** There is **no set restocking fee**, but if an
item comes back damaged, dirty or used the **refund is reduced**. Both are true at once:
- **Never write "we don't charge a restocking fee."** It's an absolute we can't always honor and
  it's the sentence that creates the argument later.
- **Never quote a fee or a number.**
- **Do tie the refund to condition, warmly:** *"Once it's back with us and checked over, we'll get
  your refund processed based on the condition it arrives in."*
- If they **ask directly:** *"There's no set restocking fee. The refund is based on the condition it
  comes back in."*

This vagueness is deliberate. It is not hedging and not something to clean up into a promise.

**Returns come back. All of them.** *(Settled by Atira 2026-08-22: "We definitely need all items
returned.")* If we're refunding, the item ships back, whatever it costs and however small. Do **not**
draft "keep it and we'll refund you anyway." The older archive has one-off keep-its. They are not
policy and not yours to reach for. **The one carve-out is not a return at all:** warranty defect
replacements and missing-item reships require nothing back.

**Don't invent concessions to soften a no.** If a customer argues the item is defective and
therefore they shouldn't pay return shipping, state the policy and process the return. Warmth comes
from acting quickly, not from giving ground nobody authorized.

**Deliver the whole return in ONE message, not three.** Conditions, the shipping deduction, the
eligible amount and what happens next all belong in the same reply.

**Process:**
1. **Troubleshoot first, or pitch the accessory that solves it.** Since Aug 2026 this comes before
   any label.
2. **Step one, before any label:** state the policy and the three conditions and ask them to
   confirm. Full refund isn't available because shipping both ways comes out. Original packaging
   with product tags attached, tested indoors only, and the reason. Multiple items all come back
   together. Closing: **Talk soon.**
3. **Step two, only once they have explicitly confirmed:** send the label and state the exact amount
   in the same message. **Write the figure as `$___`.** Never omit it because you don't have it,
   never guess. Don't ask them to agree to the figure, that's a round-trip for nothing.
   Approved shape: *"I just emailed you the labels for both strollers. Once we receive the items
   back you will be refunded. This order is eligible for a refund of $443.74."* Then the assist line
   and **Take care.**
4. **When they arrive already confirming the conditions, the two steps collapse into one message,
   and step one's explanation comes with it.** Someone writing "new in box, never used" has answered
   step one unprompted, so making them confirm again wastes a round-trip. Send the label and the
   amount. **But they have still never been told shipping comes out**, so explain the deduction in
   that same message before naming the figure. Skip the round-trip, never the explanation.
   *(Corrected by Atira 2026-08-22.)* If an earlier reply already stated the deduction, don't repeat
   it, just give the label and the amount.
5. **What counts as confirmation:** they answer the conditions. "I have the original box, tags are
   on, only used inside." **What does not count:** "I feel confident I can get it back in the box,"
   "I still have the packing," or anything about intent rather than fact.
6. Email the prepaid label. **It comes from a third-party sender and frequently lands in spam** —
   tell them to check.
7. Carts and strollers go **FedEx**, accessories go **USPS**.
8. Inspected on arrival. **Refund within 5 business days of receipt**, then 3-4 business days to
   reach their card.
9. **A chargeback stops everything.** The refund then runs through PayPal or the card issuer.

Tone: "to be eligible for a return," not "you must." Not "can you please confirm all of that,"
instead "if you can confirm all of that, just let me know and I can get a return label sent over to
you."

### Store credit and partial refunds

**Store credit is on, and it's the preferred outcome. Store credit > refund > taking it back.**
When a resolution could go either way, lead with store credit. It keeps the customer, avoids return
shipping both ways, and avoids handling a returned unit. Archive shows $249 for a discontinued cart,
full order value as an alternative to a shipping-reduced refund, and a $40 non-expiring credit.

### Exchanges and upgrades

**We don't exchange carts and strollers.** Three substitutes:
1. **Color or small-item swap:** return label plus a **$17.90 invoice** ($8.95 back + $8.95 out),
   customer pays first
2. **Upgrade offer:** **$40 off** the new V2, they keep the old cart, personalized code
3. **Cross-model swap:** pay the price difference, keep the accessory

**Car seat adapters ARE exchanged.** Standing practice from Abbey and Shad (284184228, 285584142,
223269165). **Don't assume they
ordered the wrong one** — they may have the right adapter and be installing it wrong, so the first
reply asks **which car seat they have**, not which adapter they want. The math is the $5 difference,
invoiced or refunded. Refund is the second option, and **say return shipping comes out of it before
they choose**.

**Defect replacements are different** — we ship the replacement and don't require the original back.
**A full refund on a warranty stroller requires the harness straps cut, with a photo.**

**V1 customer hits a V2-only limitation:** always include the $40 V2 upgrade alongside whatever else
you're saying. Link the **regular** page, `stroleecarts.com/products/strolee-stability-shopper`. Not a hard sell, just an option. Don't create the
code until they confirm. **Don't mention V2-only accessories to a V1 customer otherwise**, they
can't use them and it generates another ticket.

### HSA / FSA

Strolee can't apply it or process reimbursement. Through **Burst** only: `app.getburst.com` /
`support@getburst.com`.

**Raise Burst on any affordability ticket, and especially on mobility ones.** Someone saying they
can't afford the cart is the moment to mention it, not an afterthought. A cart bought for documented
mobility needs is close to the textbook case for the letter of medical necessity Burst handles.

**Can it be done AFTER the purchase? Almost never.** From `stroleecarts.com/pages/fsa-hsa`: *"An LMN
must be dated on or before the purchase date, and clinicians cannot backdate one (IRS rule)."*
**The one exception, quoted from the page:** *"if you already had an LMN dated on or before your
purchase that covers your Strolee stroller, send it through and Burst can file your claim."*

So the right answer is a question, not a flat no: **did you already have an LMN dated on or before
the day you ordered?**

**Age changes which one applies.** From 65 and certainly at 79, someone on Medicare **cannot
contribute** to an HSA but **can still spend an existing balance**, which doesn't expire. FSAs are
employer-based, so an older retired customer almost certainly doesn't have one. Say **"if you have
an HSA"** to an older customer rather than naming FSA or assuming either. Don't explain the Medicare
rule to them, it's background for us.

### Affiliates, influencers, press and wholesale

**Shopify Collabs approved affiliate.** A Collabs approval notification opening with "Your
application has been approved," carrying a link and code Shopify already generated. **Affiliates can
earn commission OR a discount**, both are on the table, so don't describe it as commission-only.
Real welcome, not a brush-off. Cover: welcome to the Strolee family, they're approved and set to
start sharing, **their actual affiliate link, their actual discount code and what it gives their
audience, and their actual commission rate, pulled from the ticket and never described
generically**, that they can share on social, blogs, stories, wherever works, and that there's no
required product. (Atira may override the "no required product" line to point someone at a specific
product. Follow her direction when she does.) Closing: **Talk soon.**

**Unsolicited influencer / creator / UGC / ambassador pitch.** A fresh inbound DM or comment
forwarded into Gorgias, subjects like "Direct message with [handle]," "Message from [name]," or a
creator describing their following. Standard answer: we don't currently have an ambassador or
partnership program but it's something we hope to bring back, and **we aren't offering gifted or
paid collaborations, only commission on sales.** Closing: **Take care.**
Application pages: `stroleecarts.com/pages/brand-ambassador` · `stroleebaby.com/pages/collab`.

**Gifting is closed.** *(Settled by Atira 2026-08-21.)* It was a real program through 2025, it isn't
now. Don't offer free product and don't hint it might be possible.

**Press and media** get the same handling as a collab pitch. No separate process exists.

**Most of this category is not spam.** The advertising tickets are mostly genuine comments on
Strolee's own ads and deserve a warm brief reply.

**Wholesale is real** and case-by-case quoting, not a published program. Never decline a bulk
request outright, ask which products and roughly what quantity, then quote.
- **3-9 carts:** accessories 35% off, Stability/pet bundle 30% off (~$182/unit)
- **10+ carts:** another 5% off (accessories 40%, bundle 35%, ~$169/unit)
- Discounts start as low as **3 units**, cap around **50% off** at high volume
- Accessories are discounted harder than carts, higher margin

**Private label** (client logo on the cart): 30% deposit, **minimum 50 units**, 45-60 day lead time.
Cheaper workaround with no stated minimum: embroider the logo on the organizer accessory only and
sell it as a bundle.

**Distribution is otherwise closed.** Our own sites, Amazon, and TikTok. Nowhere else.
**TikTok Shop: we can't do anything on that side.** Collabs codes work only on our own sites. We
can't issue TikTok Shop codes, samples or collaboration links. Say so plainly rather than offering
to look into it.

---

## PART 4 — SETTLED, AND STILL OPEN

**Consistency is the default, not a straitjacket.** These are the answers to reach for so two
customers with the same problem don't get two different answers. When a ticket genuinely warrants
more, give it more and say so in the draft. The thing to avoid is being *random*, not being generous.

**One-off exceptions do not get written down here.** When Atira approves something above the
standing amounts for a particular customer, that's a decision about that customer, not a new rule.
Recording it turns it into a precedent I'll reach for again, which is exactly how the archive's
random $10-to-$249 spread happened. *(Atira, 2026-08-22: "remove the $100 discount from the playbook
we cant offer that this is an exception.")*

The settled defaults, each with its full detail in Part 2 or 3:

- **Warranty covers manufacturer defects only, every part, no exceptions list.** Photo and order
  number first, then judge the evidence.
- **Goodwill / retention / exception: $30.** V1 upgrade: **$40.** Above that is Atira's, per ticket.
- **Store credit > refund > taking it back.**
- **Restocking: no set fee, but the refund reflects condition.** Never quote a number.
- **Cut harness strap photo: mandatory, no exceptions, ever.**
- **Porch theft: we do nothing.**
- **Returns run 30 days from delivery.** All items come back.
- **Address changes: before it ships yes, after it ships we cannot.**
- **Gifting is closed.**
- **The seated cart has no date. Be vague, every time.**
- **Open box warranty term: not tracked.** Not worth a rule.

### STILL OPEN

**Claude to research, not Atira's to answer:**
1. **Expedited shipping** — check what the website actually offers at checkout.
2. **Wheel measurements** — the diameter of the V2 Shopper wheels is published nowhere: not on the
   product page, not on the wheel pages, not anywhere in the ticket archive. Susan Armstrong asked
   on 2026-08-16. Someone has to measure one, then it goes in the WHEELS section.
2b. **Lower storage and pet seating clearance** — the height/clearance of the lower storage area,
   the height of the lower pet seating, and the drop from the bar to the lowest point of the pet
   seating are published nowhere. jade jeng asked on 2026-08-24 (ticket 289145294). Same fix as the
   wheels: someone measures a cart, then it goes in Part 2.
2c. **How the Mesh Caddy Bag attaches to a Stability Shopper** — not on the product page (which has
   **an empty description** and two `.heic` images that many browsers won't render), not on the
   how-to page, not in the ticket archive. The only recorded fact is *"It does not have a zipper
   just 2 open mesh pouches"* (ticket 279381789). Romanie Baines hit this on 2026-08-23 (ticket
   289051844). Needs Atira or Shad, then it goes in Accessories.

**Two site fixes that would stop tickets at the source, raised 2026-08-24:**
- The **Mesh Caddy Bag** product page has no description and unrenderable images.
- **Stamped review requests fire regardless of delivery status.** Yoko Arima was asked to review a
  cart that had never arrived (ticket 289031796).

**Atira's or Shad's call:**
3. **The Linq page** at `stroleecarts.com/pages/strolee-linq` is live, still says the system
   *"allow[s] families to instantly link two single strollers to form a double,"* and is **not in
   the site navigation** anywhere. Customers arrive from Google and old emails, so removing it from
   the menu would change nothing. **The page has to be edited or taken down.** That's the only thing
   that stops these tickets.
4. Does the Chicco/Graco adapter fit KeyFit Max or KeyFit Sport?
5. Does the stroller adapter fit the ORIGINAL (pre-v2) Baby+ child seat side? (Baby+ v2 basket side
   converts for a car seat or the pet bassinet. On the original Baby+, Shad told a customer Sept
   2025 the basket side only swapped with the pet bassinet.)

**Lower priority, still unsettled:**
6. **Warranty page says "no fine print"** and lists no exclusions, while pet damage, mold, wear and
   secondhand are all declined.
7. **Refund policy page says 30 days from purchase**, contradicting the delivery rule and the
   home-trial page.
8. **Restock notify-me** — every reply gives a vague ETA or points at the email list. If a real
   waitlist exists, nobody uses it.

### One warning about mining the archive yourself

**Old tickets contain replies that break current rules.** The archive has replies promising gate
check is **free of charge**, directly against the standing rule. It has "resell it on Facebook
Marketplace" as a past-window offer, now retired. It has address changes attempted with carriers
after shipping, now retired. It has "push a button to release" for wheels, which is wrong.
**Mine the archive for facts and policy. Never for voice, and never assume a past reply was correct.**

---

## PART 5 — HOW THIS FILE STAYS GOOD

This file grew to 1,300 lines in a day and started contradicting itself, which produced a bad draft.
Four rules keep that from happening again.

**1. One topic, one home.** Wheels live in the WHEELS section. Restock rules live in Restocks and
Launches. Warranty lives in Warranty. If you're about to state a rule in a second place, don't.
Link to the section instead. Before adding anything, `grep` for it first.

**2. Put the rule in, leave the story out.** "Corrected by Atira after I told two customers no video
existed" is a mistake log, not knowledge. Keep the rule, keep a short attribution where it
establishes authority, drop the narration. The *why* survives only where it changes what a customer
gets told, like the frame-stability answer for V1 owners.

**3. A correction that contradicts an existing line replaces that line.** It does not get appended
underneath it. Two rules on one topic in one file is the failure mode, not the safeguard. Where the
replacement changes the meaning of a hard requirement, show Atira the before and after rather than
doing it silently.

**4. Requirements are never reworded, softened or "clarified."** The order-number requirement, the
cut-harness-strap photo, the original-box rule, the 30-day window. Those get quoted exactly. If one
looks wrong, say so to Atira and leave it as it is.

**Where things go:** a fact or policy goes here. A voice correction goes in CLAUDE.md. A scenario
requirement goes in CHECKS.md as a check, because prose gets skimmed and checks get run. A
correction about how the work is done goes in the skill file.

**Anything looked up that wasn't here gets added in the same session.** The next session should
never re-look-up something this one already found.
